{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (Phase 1 complete — proven root cause, runtime-confirmed)\n\nSTALE CITATION IN THIS TICKET: the description points at\n`adapters/jira/transport.py:379-416`. Ticket 465d's one-module-per-capability split has since\nlanded; `_paged_search` now lives at\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py:120-157`\n(class `_TransportBase`, the shared pager every capability mixin inherits). The defect moved\nwith it verbatim.\n\nROOT CAUSE (two coupled mechanisms, one artifact each):\n\nM1 — the pager loop has no offset-stall guard. `_base.py:141-157`:\n\n    out = []; start_at = 0\n    while True:\n        results = _call_logged(\"_paged_search\", jql, lambda offset=start_at: ...)\n        batch = [_unwrap(i) for i in results]\n        if not batch: break          # <-- the ONLY exit\n        out.extend(batch)\n        start_at += len(batch)\n\n`start_at` advances locally, but nothing checks that the SERVER honoured it. A DC instance\nthat ignores/repeats `startAt` re-serves the same non-empty page forever, so `batch` is never\nempty and the only exit is unreachable: an unbounded loop with `out` growing without limit.\n\nM2 — the fail-open handler would swallow a loud abort. `_hierarchy.py:91`\n(`get_parent_map`) wraps the `_paged_search` drain in a bare\n`except Exception: log warning; return {}` degradation contract. Any error the pager raises is\nconverted into a silent EMPTY parent map — i.e. the loud signal M1's fix adds would be\nneutralised at this caller unless it is re-raised ahead of the broad clause, exactly as the\nCloud sibling does (`adapters/jira/acli_graph.py:304-306, 394-396, 477`).\n\nDISCRIMINATING RUNTIME EVIDENCE (not static reading — the hypothesis is dynamic):\n\nExperiment 1 (M1) — drove the real `_paged_search` with a `startAt`-ignoring stub that serves\nthe same 3-issue page for every request, plus a 25-call harness cap to bound the run:\n  RESULT: 26 calls. Offsets REQUESTED = [0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27, ...] — the client\n  kept advancing while the server kept serving page 1. Terminated only by the harness cap, not\n  by the pager. Predicted-if-true outcome exactly; a guarded pager would have stopped at 2.\n\nExperiment 2 (M2) — same stub through `get_parent_map`:\n  RESULT: returned `{}` after 26 calls, raising nothing. Confirms the fail-open path is live\n  and converts a pager-level abort into a silent empty map (the differ then treats every issue\n  as parentless).\n\nAlternatives ruled out: not `_call_logged`/retry (it re-raises untouched, `_base.py:60-66`);\nnot the short-page/truncation defect (bug 9263 — that one is already fixed here and the\noffsets prove the loop IS advancing its request, so the failure is server-side offset\nblindness, a different axis); not a caller-side loop (all three callers drain the shared pager,\n`_links.py:39`, `_links.py:87`, `_hierarchy.py:78` — there is exactly one loop).\n\nLEGITIMACY = defect, against three cited authorities in this same codebase:\n1. `fetcher.py:336-344` — the SAME operation (offset-paged whole-project issue search) on a\n   parallel surface RAISES `SilentTruncationError(reason=\"offset-stall\")` on exactly this\n   condition, and states the rule as a documented contract at `fetcher.py:275-277`. Design\n   invariant.\n2. `adapters/jira/acli_graph.py:29-46, 79-86` — the Cloud sibling raises\n   `RunawayPaginationError` on a stalled cursor and its readers re-raise past their fail-open\n   handlers. Prior CLOSED `Fixed:` bug cabc-7a98-d173-4d7c for this same class (commit\n   30c522cde9).\n3. `_base.py:131-139` — this pager's own docstring claims a structural test prevents a further\n   unguarded instance of the class; that guard covers only the page-size axis, not offset stall.\n\nPARITY CENSUS (Step-7 Axis 2) — rule: \"an offset/cursor-paged whole-project search must abort\nloudly when the server stops advancing\":\n- `fetcher._iter_pages` (offset)          -> HOLDS, `fetcher.py:336-344`\n- `acli_graph._iter_cursor_pages` (cursor) -> HOLDS, `acli_graph.py:79-86`\n- `jira_datacenter/_base._paged_search`    -> **MISSING** (this ticket)\n- `_issues.py:257-263` / `acli.py:448`     -> N/A: single-page primitives, not pagers; the\n  loop that drives them is `fetcher._iter_pages`, already guarded.\nExactly one MISSING slot. No further siblings.\n\nCALLER-DEPENDENCY GATE: callers are `get_issuelinks_map` (`_links.py:39`), `get_comment_map`\n(`_links.py:87`), `get_parent_map` (`_hierarchy.py:78`). None depends on the spin. The one\ndeliberate behaviour change is M2 — `get_parent_map` stops fail-opening on a stall — which is\nacceptance criterion 2 and matches the Cloud precedent. Gate passes.\n\nFIX PLAN (narrow by design; ticket 465d owns re-architecting these modules and another stream\nowns `set_parent`/parent handling, so the diff stays minimal):\n1. `_base.py` — add a dedicated `RunawayPaginationError(RuntimeError)` beside the pager, and\n   track the previous page's first issue key in `_paged_search`. If a page repeats the previous\n   page's first key, raise it: the server is not honouring `startAt`, so paging can never\n   advance. Raises on the SECOND call.\n   DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE from `fetcher.py:335-345`: fetcher returns cleanly (no raise) when the\n   repeated page is SHORT, reasoning that a client returning fewer items than asked and then\n   repeating itself \"has nothing further to give\". That reasoning does NOT transfer to DC. This\n   pager exists (bug 9263) precisely because a hardened DC caps EVERY page below the requested\n   size via `jira.search.views.default.max` — so on DC a short page is the NORMAL case with more\n   to give, and adopting fetcher's short-page branch would silently return 20 of 250 (the exact\n   92%-loss defect this pager was built to refuse). `_paged_search` therefore raises on ANY\n   repeated page, short or full. It cannot false-positive: a `startAt`-honouring server serves\n   DIFFERENT issues at each offset.\n2. `_hierarchy.py` — add `except RunawayPaginationError: raise` immediately ahead of\n   `get_parent_map`'s broad `except Exception`, mirroring `acli_graph.py:304-306`.\n3. `transport.py` — re-export the error through the existing `__all__` facade (2 lines only;\n   no other change to that file).\n4. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py` — the RED oracle: a\n   `startAt`-ignoring stub proving loud self-termination within 2 calls, that the error escapes\n   `get_parent_map`'s fail-open, and that well-behaved page-capping servers still recover 250/250."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785882790042713001,"uuid":"c0c69a63-55ba-4696-ac31-db17fa392cf7"}